1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,800
This is Orbita — an AI assistant for meetings, tasks and notes. Home page: getorbita.me, with links to our Privacy Policy and Terms.

2
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,800
The user is signed in to Orbita and opens Profile → Google Calendar to connect their Google account.

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,800
The user clicks Connect Google Calendar.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,800
Google's consent screen. The OAuth client ID is visible in the address bar.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,800
Orbita requests two scopes: Google Calendar and Google Tasks. The user grants access.

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,800
Access granted. The user returns to Orbita.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:01:20,800
calendar scope: Orbita shows the user's schedule from Google Calendar.

8
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:56,800
calendar scope: at the user's request, Leo creates an event and invites the attendee.

9
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:14,800
The event appears in the user's Google Calendar.

10
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:39,800
calendar scope: rescheduling at the user's request.

11
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:59,800
calendar scope: finding free time across the user's calendars.

12
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:45,800
tasks scope: tasks created in Orbita appear in the user's Google Tasks.

13
00:03:46,000 --> 00:04:00,800
Completing the task in Google Tasks marks it done in Orbita.

14
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:25,800
calendar scope: cancelling an event at the user's request.

15
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:34,800
The user can disconnect Google at any time; Orbita deletes the access tokens.

16
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Access can also be revoked in the Google Account settings.
